# Schema: Polkadot SDK PRDoc Schema (prdoc) v1.0.0
# See doc at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/master/prdoc/schema_user.json

title: "pallet-assets: allow a privileged origin to declare ED-independent (persistent) accounts"

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |-
      Adds the ability for `ForceOrigin` to mark an asset-account as *persistent*. A persistent
      account exists independent of the existential deposit: it is never reaped for holding a
      balance below the asset's `min_balance`. This is useful for system accounts such as pallet
      pots that must keep existing even when emptied, without resorting to minting dust to keep
      them alive.

      New extrinsics:
      - `force_set_persistent(id, who)`: marks `who` as persistent, creating the asset-account if it
        does not exist yet. Accounts backed by a deposit (`DepositHeld`/`DepositFrom`) are rejected.
      - `force_unset_persistent(id, who)`: removes the persistent mark. A zero-balance account is
        reaped, an account holding at least `min_balance` is demoted to a regular existence reason,
        and a non-zero sub-minimal balance is rejected (it would have to be burned).

      A new `ExistenceReason::Persistent` variant is added to model this state, together with the
      `AccountPersistenceSet`/`AccountPersistenceRemoved` events and the `AlreadyPersistent`,
      `NotPersistent` and `AccountHasDeposit` errors.

crates:
  - name: pallet-assets
    bump: major
